```
Reason:
The condition checks if the `new_view` is of type `C_OUTPUT`, which incorrectly allows the focus to be set to the output itself instead of the associated workspace. This behavior prevents users from effectively switching between outputs, especially when a workspace with children is selected.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
} else if (new_view->type == C_OUTPUT) {
    return set_focused_container(swayc_active_workspace_for(new_view));
```
Reason:
This change ensures that when the `new_view` is of type `C_OUTPUT`, the focus is set to the workspace associated with that output instead of the output itself. This corrects the functionality, allowing users to switch between outputs as expected.

